","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7829","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7829","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7829.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7829.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-08T22:20:40Z"},"body":"Follow-up to #7820 (merged): fixes a `NameError` that killed the yard reaper's first real `--apply` run before anything was reaped (the entry loop referenced `root`, which only exists inside `discover_entries`). Caught by running the bounded first pass on the live yard; the run failed safe — zero entries moved, zero bytes deleted, `plan` record intact in the run log.\n\nAlso adds `MainApplyTests`: end-to-end `main()` coverage on a synthetic yard (liveness sources mocked) asserting an eligible entry is moved to trash, a keep-set entry is untouched, and the log carries `reap-start`/`reaped`/`summary`. The classification-only suite is why this escaped; that gap is now closed. 17 tests pass locally.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796768411&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7829&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7829&signature=b64bbb3c631b6fd5bbf46e6269284a7140410c23576b97ee728e2186df9ba8d1\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture